intent: "ES1 P3.5 SHIPPED 2026-06-02 — S-12 speculative driver NOW CONSUMES X3.5 PROVE verdicts. New closure-injectable helper `filter_by_proof<F>(candidates, claim, ctx, backend, prove_closure: F)` at speculative.rs:123 inserted as a pre-pass before `rank_by_predicted` in `run_gateway_speculative` (pre_exec.rs:295). The X3.5 PROVE substrate (delivered in P3) is now *used*: proven claims inform accept-prefix decisions, defense-in-depth against Unsat (claim proven false = candidate invalid) and Error (encoder/solver fail) at the earliest possible point. 8 new tests (5 unit in speculative.rs + 3 integration in pre_exec.rs). 2 primary files modified (speculative.rs 399 LOC + pre_exec.rs 1197 LOC) + 1 P3 LEFTOVER fix (touring-server/src/cli/exec.rs:5 GatewayDeps struct literals at L152, L354, L485, L698, L1072 — unfazed by P3 type-def change; caught at FASE 0 cargo check --workspace 5 E0063 errors; fixed by adding the 3 X3.5 fields claim/claim_context/solver_backend). 3966/3966 touring-hooks lib tests pass (was 3958, +8 net), 118 ceg_e2e + 2 capnp_embed_e2e PASS. 0 regressions, 0 new orphans. 2.0ed consumed of 3 budget. Stub->Void contract preserved. CAH conformance: `interface.formal-verify` 0.65 -> CONFORME expected ~0.85+ after oracle re-run (matches P1+P4/P2/P3 predictions). HONEST SCOPE: (1) Stub->Void = NEUTRAL filter (candidates KEPT, NOT rejected); (2) opt-in: claim=None returns input unchanged (zero overhead for default callers, lossless contract preserved); (3) closure-injectable F parameter enables deterministic status testing without touching production wiring; (4) P3 leftover = META-LESSON that type-def change is not update-all-callsites — FASE 0 (cargo check --workspace) is the canonical gate for type-def changes."
