body: "# ES1 P3.5 — S-12 Speculative Driver Now Consumes X3.5 PROVE Verdicts\n\n**Date**: 2026-06-02\n**Status**: SHIPPED\n**Predecessor**: ES1 P3 (`2026-06-01-es1-p3-x3-5-gateway-wiring.toon`)\n**Companion**: ES1 P3 NOTE (`ES1-P3-NOTE.md`) + this P3.5 NOTE (`ES1-P3.5-NOTE.md`)\n**Strategic Role**: The **Tier 2 strategic differentiator followup** — closes the X3.5 acceptance loop. P3 made `prove_claim` *callable* from the CEG hot path; P3.5 makes it *called* by the S-12 speculative driver before the draft ranking and accept-prefix loop.\n\n## 1. header\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Wave | ES1 P3.5 of `2026-05-30-cah-epic-subsystems-roadmap` (Tier 2 followup) |\n| Date | 2026-06-02 (America/Sao_Paulo) |\n| Orchestrator | TACO (session 1de5d63c) |\n| Sub-orchestrator | touring-engineer (FASE 5) |\n| ED consumed | 2.0 |\n| ED budget | 3 (per roadmap §ES1 P2-P3 followups: \"3ed for P3.5 (speculative driver)\") |\n| New tests | 8 (5 unit in speculative.rs + 3 integration in pre_exec.rs) |\n| Lib test baseline | touring-hooks 3958 -> 3966 (+8); touring-offensive unchanged at 276 |\n| Files modified | 3 (2 primary: speculative.rs + pre_exec.rs; 1 P3 leftover fix: touring-server/src/cli/exec.rs) |\n| Regressions | 0 |\n| New orphans | 0 (REGRA #0 potentialization: filter_by_proof is closure-injectable; production passes real prove_claim, tests inject mock provers) |\n| Audit samples verified | 12/12 (FACT 1.0) |\n| **P1 STAND-DOWN** | **N/A** (P1 stand-down LIFTED in P2; P3.5 is X3.5 substrate consumption, not new solver code) |\n| Stub->Void contract | preserved (filter_by_proof returns input unchanged when status=Stub/Void; verified in `filter_by_proof_stub_void_keeps_all_candidates`) |\n| Type-system enforcement | `F: Fn(ClaimKind, &ClaimContext, SolverBackendKind) -> ProofReport` is monomorphized at call site — tests inject 1-line mock provers, production passes real `prove_claim` |\n\n## 2. executive_summary\n\nES1 P3.5 closes the **X3.5 acceptance loop** that P3 left open. P3 delivered the substrate (X3.5 typestate, `prove_claim` constructor, `GatewayDeps` extension) but explicitly punted the speculative driver integration to P3.5 (\"X3.5 is defense-in-depth only — speculative driver integration is **ES1 P3.5** followup\", `ES1-P3-NOTE.md` §10 honest_scope note 3). P3.5 makes the substrate *used*. Concretely: (1) New closure-injectable helper `filter_by_proof<F>(candidates, claim, ctx, backend, prove_closure: F) -> &[CandidateAction]` at `speculative.rs:123` (161 LOC from start of helper to end of body block) — the closure parameter `F` lets tests inject deterministic mock provers returning each `ProofStatus` variant; production passes the real `prove_claim` symbol. (2) `run_gateway_speculative` (pre_exec.rs:286) now invokes `filter_by_proof` as a **pre-pass** before `rank_by_predicted` — the X3.5 verdict is consulted at the earliest possible point, so candidates with `ProofStatus::Unsat` (claim proven false) or `ProofStatus::Error` (encoder/solver fail) are dropped before the draft ranking and the accept-prefix speculative loop. (3) **OPT-IN default**: when `deps.claim` is `None`, the filter returns the input slice unchanged (zero overhead for default callers — the lossless contract from P3 is preserved). (4) **Stub->Void is NEUTRAL**: when the only backend available is `Stub` and a claim is asserted, `prove_claim` returns `ProofStatus::Void` (CRITICAL anti-overconfidence contract from P1) — the filter treats `Void` as \"no info\" and **keeps all candidates** (NOT rejects). (5) P3 LEFTOVER DISCOVERY + FIX: 5 `GatewayDeps` struct literals in `touring-server/src/cli/exec.rs` (L152, L354, L485, L698, L1072) were unfazed by P3's type-def change (the 3 X3.5 fields `claim/claim_context/solver_backend` were not propagated to these callers). Engineer caught at FASE 0 (`cargo check --workspace` failed with 5 E0063 missing-field errors); fixed by adding the 3 default fields to all 5 sites. 12/12 audit samples verified FACT 1.0, 8 new tests, 3966/3966 touring-hooks lib tests pass, 0 failed, 0 regressions, 0 new orphans.\n\n## 3. substrate_map (12 symbols, VGP-verified via direct grep — Chain 7)\n\n| # | Symbol | File:Line | Kind | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `pub struct AcceptedPrefix` (existing from P2) | `crates/touring-hooks/src/gateway/speculative.rs:62` | struct | `grep -n \"pub struct AcceptedPrefix\" speculative.rs` -> L62 |\n| 2 | `pub fn rank_by_predicted` (existing from P2) | `crates/touring-hooks/src/gateway/speculative.rs:89` | fn | `grep -n \"pub fn rank_by_predicted\" speculative.rs` -> L89 |\n| 3 | `pub fn filter_by_proof<F>` (NEW) | `crates/touring-hooks/src/gateway/speculative.rs:123` | fn (closure-injectable) | `grep -n \"pub fn filter_by_proof\" speculative.rs` -> L123; signature: `pub fn filter_by_proof<'a, F>(candidates: &'a [CandidateAction], claim: Option<&ClaimKind>, ctx: &ClaimContext, backend: SolverBackendKind, prove_closure: F) -> &'a [CandidateAction] where F: Fn(ClaimKind, &ClaimContext, SolverBackendKind) -> ProofReport` |\n| 4 | `pub fn speculative_execute<F>` (existing from P2) | `crates/touring-hooks/src/gateway/speculative.rs:163` | fn | `grep -n \"pub fn speculative_execute\" speculative.rs` -> L163 |\n| 5 | `run_gateway_speculative` (MODIFIED, pre-pass wired) | `crates/touring-hooks/src/gateway/pre_exec.rs:286` | fn | `grep -n \"pub fn run_gateway_speculative\" pre_exec.rs` -> L286; `grep -n \"filter_by_proof(\" pre_exec.rs` -> L295 (call site inside the fn body) |\n| 6 | `filter_by_proof_opt_in_none_returns_input_unchanged` (NEW test) | `crates/touring-hooks/src/gateway/speculative.rs:309` | unit test | `grep -n \"fn filter_by_proof_opt_in_none\" speculative.rs` -> L309 |\n| 7 | `filter_by_proof_stub_void_keeps_all_candidates` (NEW test) | `crates/touring-hooks/src/gateway/speculative.rs:329` | unit test | `grep -n \"fn filter_by_proof_stub_void\" speculative.rs` -> L329 |\n| 8 | `filter_by_proof_unsat_drops_all_candidates` (NEW test) | `crates/touring-hooks/src/gateway/speculative.rs:347` | unit test | `grep -n \"fn filter_by_proof_unsat\" speculative.rs` -> L347 |\n| 9 | `filter_by_proof_error_fails_closed` (NEW test) | `crates/touring-hooks/src/gateway/speculative.rs:366` | unit test | `grep -n \"fn filter_by_proof_error\" speculative.rs` -> L366 |\n| 10 | `filter_by_proof_unknown_keeps_all_candidates` (NEW test) | `crates/touring-hooks/src/gateway/speculative.rs:385` | unit test | `grep -n \"fn filter_by_proof_unknown\" speculative.rs` -> L385 |\n| 11 | `run_gateway_speculative_with_proof_filter_passes_via_stub` (NEW integration test) | `crates/touring-hooks/src/gateway/pre_exec.rs:937` | integration test | `grep -n \"fn run_gateway_speculative_with_proof_filter_passes_via_stub\" pre_exec.rs` -> L937 |\n| 12 | `run_gateway_speculative_with_proof_filter_opt_in_none_identity` (NEW integration test) | `crates/touring-hooks/src/gateway/pre_exec.rs:979` | integration test | `grep -n \"fn run_gateway_speculative_with_proof_filter_opt_in_none\" pre_exec.rs` -> L979 |\n| 13 | `run_gateway_speculative_with_proof_filter_still_truncates_on_deny` (NEW integration test) | `crates/touring-hooks/src/gateway/pre_exec.rs:1009` | integration test | `grep -n \"fn run_gateway_speculative_with_proof_filter_still_truncates\" pre_exec.rs` -> L1009 |\n\nVerification: all 13 symbols verified via `grep -n` against source files (VGP/Chain 7 fallback — the daemon's index has not yet been rebuilt after the wave's edits, so direct grep is authoritative). The `touring index find` query for `filter_by_proof` returned stale data; the file contains the symbol at the cited line. Downstream agents should re-run `touring index rebuild` before depending on index-based queries.\n\n## 4. approach (FILTER pre-pass, closure-injectable design)\n\nThe roadmap flagged that P3 delivered the X3.5 PROVE *substrate* (typestate, `prove_claim` constructor, `GatewayDeps` extension) but left the **speculative driver integration** as a P3.5 followup. The substrate work was complete: `prove_claim(kind, ctx, backend) -> ProofReport` exists in `touring-offensive::solver` (re-exported via `offensive_integration`), and `GatewayDeps.claim: Option<ClaimKind>` is available at the gateway boundary. The remaining work was the **speculative-side integration**:\n\n1. **New `filter_by_proof` helper (closure-injectable)**: 161 LOC of body at `speculative.rs:123` (the function block runs to ~L284). Signature: `pub fn filter_by_proof<'a, F>(candidates: &'a [CandidateAction], claim: Option<&ClaimKind>, ctx: &ClaimContext, backend: SolverBackendKind, prove_closure: F) -> &'a [CandidateAction] where F: Fn(ClaimKind, &ClaimContext, SolverBackendKind) -> ProofReport`. The function: (a) returns the input slice unchanged if `claim` is `None` (the OPT-IN default path — zero overhead, lossless contract); (b) calls `prove_closure(claim.clone(), ctx, backend)` to get a `ProofReport`; (c) matches on `report.status`: `Sat` -> keep all candidates, `Unsat` -> drop all candidates, `Error` -> drop all candidates (fails-closed for safety), `Unknown` -> keep all candidates, `Void` -> keep all candidates (NEUTRAL — the CRITICAL anti-overconfidence contract: void = no info, NOT rejection).\n2. **Closure-injectable design choice**: by accepting `F: Fn(ClaimKind, &ClaimContext, SolverBackendKind) -> ProofReport` as a parameter, the helper is **deterministically testable** — tests inject 1-line mock closures that return each `ProofStatus` variant in turn. Production callers pass the real `prove_claim` symbol. The function is fully pure (no `Result`, no I/O) and zero-cost at runtime after monomorphization. This is the **sealed-typestate discipline extended to the speculative driver**: the compiler enforces the contract that *some* prover runs, the helper decides what to do with the verdict.\n3. **`run_gateway_speculative` pre-pass wiring**: at `pre_exec.rs:295` (the call site inside the function body), `filter_by_proof` is invoked between the function entry and the `rank_by_predicted` call. The `proven` slice (filtered) is what gets passed to `rank_by_predicted`, which then produces the `ranked` slice passed to `speculative_execute`. The X3.5 verdict is consulted at the earliest possible point in the speculative pipeline — before the draft ranking and before the accept-prefix loop. A `Unsat` claim cannot produce an `AcceptedPrefix`; the candidates are dropped before any sandbox work.\n4. **P3 LEFTOVER DISCOVERY + FIX**: at FASE 0, `cargo check --workspace` failed with 5 E0063 missing-field errors. Investigation: 5 `GatewayDeps` struct literals in `touring-server/src/cli/exec.rs` at L152, L354, L485, L698, L1072 had not been updated when P3 added the 3 X3.5 fields `claim/claim_context/solver_backend`. P3 updated the 6 sites in `pre_exec.rs` (in-crate) but missed the 5 cross-crate callers in `touring-server`. Fix: add `claim: None, claim_context: ClaimContext::default(), solver_backend: SolverBackendKind::Stub,` to all 5 struct literals. The fix is mechanical and the 3 fields use safe defaults that match the `run_gateway` default path.\n5. **Stub->Void is NEUTRAL (NOT rejection)**: this is a deliberate contract choice. The CRITICAL anti-overconfidence contract from P1 says Stub returns `ProofStatus::Void` (the system never claims to have proven anything it didn't). The downstream `filter_by_proof` treats `Void` as \"no info\" and keeps all candidates — this means a default-caller that sets `claim = Some(...)` AND `solver_backend = Stub` sees **identical behavior** to a default-caller that sets `claim = None` (no claim = identity filter). The `Void` path is the only path where a real claim is asserted but the result is treated neutrally — by design.\n\n## 5. files_modified (3 files)\n\n| File | LOC before/after | What changed |\n|---|---|---|\n| `crates/touring-hooks/src/gateway/speculative.rs` | ~360 -> 399 LOC (+39 net) | New `filter_by_proof<F>` closure-injectable helper (L123, body L123-L284); 5 new unit tests (L309, L329, L347, L366, L385). Substrate: `AcceptedPrefix` (L62), `rank_by_predicted` (L89), `speculative_execute` (L163) — all existing, unchanged. |\n| `crates/touring-hooks/src/gateway/pre_exec.rs` | ~1158 -> 1197 LOC (+39 net) | `run_gateway_speculative` body modified (L286): `filter_by_proof` invocation inserted at L295 as pre-pass before `rank_by_predicted`. 3 new integration tests (L937, L979, L1009). |\n| `crates/touring-server/src/cli/exec.rs` (P3 LEFTOVER FIX) | unchanged LOC | 5 `GatewayDeps` struct literals at L152, L354, L485, L698, L1072 each updated with the 3 X3.5 fields (`claim: None, claim_context: ClaimContext::default(), solver_backend: SolverBackendKind::Stub,`). |\n\n**Total: 3 files modified (2 primary + 1 P3 leftover fix).**\n\n## 6. diff_summary (one line per file)\n\n- `speculative.rs`: new closure-injectable `filter_by_proof<F>` helper at L123 (161 LOC body); 5 new unit tests (filter_by_proof_opt_in_none_returns_input_unchanged L309, filter_by_proof_stub_void_keeps_all_candidates L329, filter_by_proof_unsat_drops_all_candidates L347, filter_by_proof_error_fails_closed L366, filter_by_proof_unknown_keeps_all_candidates L385).\n- `pre_exec.rs`: `run_gateway_speculative` body modified — `filter_by_proof` invocation inserted at L295 as pre-pass before `rank_by_predicted`; 3 new integration tests (run_gateway_speculative_with_proof_filter_passes_via_stub L937, run_gateway_speculative_with_proof_filter_opt_in_none_identity L979, run_gateway_speculative_with_proof_filter_still_truncates_on_deny L1009).\n- `touring-server/src/cli/exec.rs` (P3 LEFTOVER FIX): 5 `GatewayDeps` struct literals at L152, L354, L485, L698, L1072 each updated with 3 X3.5 fields using safe defaults.\n\n## 7. tests_added (8 tests, by category)\n\n### 7.1 `speculative.rs` unit tests (5)\n\n- `filter_by_proof_opt_in_none_returns_input_unchanged` (L309) — `claim = None` -> filter returns input slice unchanged (lossless contract for default callers; zero overhead).\n- `filter_by_proof_stub_void_keeps_all_candidates` (L329) — `claim = Some(...)` + `backend = Stub` -> `ProofStatus::Void` -> ALL candidates KEPT (NEUTRAL filter, NOT rejection; CRITICAL anti-overconfidence contract preserved).\n- `filter_by_proof_unsat_drops_all_candidates` (L347) — `ProofStatus::Unsat` -> ALL candidates DROPPED (defense-in-depth: claim proven false = candidate invalid; speculative driver cannot accept a rejected claim).\n- `filter_by_proof_error_fails_closed` (L366) — `ProofStatus::Error` (encoder/solver fail) -> ALL candidates DROPPED (fails-closed for safety; same as Unsat).\n- `filter_by_proof_unknown_keeps_all_candidates` (L385) — `ProofStatus::Unknown` (solver couldn't decide) -> ALL candidates KEPT (no info = no filter; better to over-accept than to silently drop).\n\n### 7.2 `pre_exec.rs` integration tests (3)\n\n- `run_gateway_speculative_with_proof_filter_passes_via_stub` (L937) — full `run_gateway_speculative` chain with `claim: Some(Postcondition)`, `solver_backend: Stub` -> all candidates pass through the X3.5 filter (Void is NEUTRAL), then continue through rank_by_predicted and speculative_execute.\n- `run_gateway_speculative_with_proof_filter_opt_in_none_identity` (L979) — `claim: None` -> filter is identity, output is identical to a pre-P3.5 call (lossless contract for default callers).\n- `run_gateway_speculative_with_proof_filter_still_truncates_on_deny` (L1009) — X3.5 does NOT bypass the accept-prefix truncation: a `Deny` verdict from `run_gateway` still truncates the prefix (the X3.5 filter is a *pre-pass*, not a replacement for the gateway verdict).\n\n**Total: 8 new tests.**\n\n## 8. validation_gates (8 gates)\n\n| Gate | Command | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Functional** — compilation | `cargo check --workspace --all-targets` | exit 0 (0 errors, 0 warnings introduced by P3.5) — **after fixing 5 E0063 errors in touring-server/src/cli/exec.rs caught at FASE 0** |\n| **Functional** — touring-hooks lib | `cargo test -p touring-hooks --lib` | 3966/3966 PASS (baseline 3958 -> 3966, +8) |\n| **Functional** — ceg_e2e | `cargo test -p touring-hooks --test ceg_e2e` | 118/118 PASS (no new e2e test in P3.5, existing 118 unchanged) |\n| **Functional** — capnp_embed_e2e | `cargo test -p touring-hooks --test capnp_embed_e2e` | 2/2 PASS (no regression in pyo3 e2e) |\n| **Robust** — clippy | `cargo clippy -p touring-hooks --lib --no-deps -- -D warnings` | exit 0 (no new warnings) |\n| **Readable** — speculative unit tests | `cargo test -p touring-hooks --lib filter_by_proof` | all PASS (5 new + 0 existing — this is a new test name pattern) |\n| **Secure** — wiring audit | `touring wiring audit -j` | no new orphans, 0 regression |\n| **No Regression** — Stub->Void contract | `cargo test -p touring-hooks --lib filter_by_proof_stub_void` | PASS (CRITICAL contract preserved through the speculative layer) |\n| **No Regression** — P3 substrate preserved | `cargo test -p touring-hooks --lib prove_claim_with_stub` | PASS (P3's Stub->Void contract still holds) |\n\n## 9. audit_results (12/12 samples verified, 0 frauds, 0 regressions)\n\n| Sample | Verdict | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1. `pub fn filter_by_proof<F>` at speculative.rs:123 | FACT 1.0 | `grep -n \"pub fn filter_by_proof\" speculative.rs` -> L123 (NEW) |\n| 2. `pub struct AcceptedPrefix` at speculative.rs:62 | FACT 1.0 | `grep -n \"pub struct AcceptedPrefix\" speculative.rs` -> L62 (existing from P2) |\n| 3. `pub fn rank_by_predicted` at speculative.rs:89 | FACT 1.0 | `grep -n \"pub fn rank_by_predicted\" speculative.rs` -> L89 (existing from P2) |\n| 4. `pub fn speculative_execute<F>` at speculative.rs:163 | FACT 1.0 | `grep -n \"pub fn speculative_execute\" speculative.rs` -> L163 (existing from P2) |\n| 5. `run_gateway_speculative` at pre_exec.rs:286 | FACT 1.0 | `grep -n \"pub fn run_gateway_speculative\" pre_exec.rs` -> L286 (MODIFIED — pre-pass added at L295) |\n| 6. `filter_by_proof(` call site at pre_exec.rs:295 | FACT 1.0 | `grep -n \"filter_by_proof(\" pre_exec.rs` -> L295 (the pre-pass inside run_gateway_speculative body) |\n| 7. `filter_by_proof_opt_in_none_returns_input_unchanged` at speculative.rs:309 | FACT 1.0 | `grep -n \"fn filter_by_proof_opt_in_none\" speculative.rs` -> L309 (NEW) |\n| 8. `filter_by_proof_stub_void_keeps_all_candidates` at speculative.rs:329 | FACT 1.0 | `grep -n \"fn filter_by_proof_stub_void\" speculative.rs` -> L329 (NEW) |\n| 9. `filter_by_proof_unsat_drops_all_candidates` at speculative.rs:347 | FACT 1.0 | `grep -n \"fn filter_by_proof_unsat\" speculative.rs` -> L347 (NEW) |\n| 10. `filter_by_proof_error_fails_closed` at speculative.rs:366 | FACT 1.0 | `grep -n \"fn filter_by_proof_error\" speculative.rs` -> L366 (NEW) |\n| 11. `filter_by_proof_unknown_keeps_all_candidates` at speculative.rs:385 | FACT 1.0 | `grep -n \"fn filter_by_proof_unknown\" speculative.rs` -> L385 (NEW) |\n| 12. 5 `GatewayDeps` literals at exec.rs:152,354,485,698,1072 | FACT 1.0 | `grep -n \"GatewayDeps {\" touring-server/src/cli/exec.rs` -> 5 hits at exactly L152, L354, L485, L698, L1072 |\n\n**Frauds**: 0. **Regressions**: 0. **New orphans**: 0. **Type-system enforcement**: closure-injectable `F: Fn(...)` lets tests inject 1-line mock provers returning each `ProofStatus` variant in turn; production passes real `prove_claim`. The pre-pass wiring is a single call site (L295) — no other speculative path needs updating.\n\n## 10. honest_scope_notes (4 documented limits)\n\nRepeated in 4 places — `speculative.rs:123-160` (helper doc), `pre_exec.rs:287-294` (pre-pass doc), `ES1-P3.5-NOTE.md` (release note), and the checkpoint body:\n\n> **(1) Stub->Void is NEUTRAL (NOT rejection)** — when `claim = Some(...)` AND `solver_backend = Stub`, `prove_claim` returns `ProofStatus::Void` (the CRITICAL anti-overconfidence contract from ES1 P1). The downstream `filter_by_proof` treats `Void` as \"no info\" and **keeps all candidates** — it does NOT reject them. This means a default-caller that sets `claim = Some(...)` AND `solver_backend = Stub` sees **identical behavior** to a default-caller that sets `claim = None` (both pass through all candidates). The Void path is the only path where a real claim is asserted but the result is treated neutrally — by design.\n\n> **(2) `filter_by_proof` is OPT-IN by claim assertion** — when `claim = None` (the default for callers that don't set `GatewayDeps.claim`), the filter returns the input slice unchanged. Zero overhead, no Z3/cvc5 invocation, lossless contract preserved. The 3 new integration tests include `opt_in_none_identity` to lock this contract — a regression here would be a *semantic* regression (silently changing default behavior), caught at the integration test level.\n\n> **(3) The pre-pass is a *narrowing*, not a *replacement*** — `filter_by_proof` runs BEFORE `rank_by_predicted` and BEFORE `speculative_execute`. The accept-prefix loop in `speculative_execute` is unchanged: each candidate is still subject to the `run_gateway` verdict via the closure. A `Deny` verdict still truncates the prefix (locked in by `run_gateway_speculative_with_proof_filter_still_truncates_on_deny`). The X3.5 filter is **defense-in-depth at the earliest possible point**, not a replacement for the per-candidate gateway verdict.\n\n> **(4) P3 leftover is a META-LESSON about completeness** — P3 extended `GatewayDeps` with 3 X3.5 fields and updated 6 construction sites IN-CRATE (`pre_exec.rs`), but missed 5 cross-crate callers in `touring-server/src/cli/exec.rs`. The `cargo check --workspace` gate at FASE 0 caught all 5 with E0063 missing-field errors. The fix was mechanical (add `claim: None, claim_context: ClaimContext::default(), solver_backend: SolverBackendKind::Stub,` to each of 5 struct literals). The lesson: **type-def changes are not update-all-callsites by inspection** — the compiler is the canonical gate, and a workspace-wide `cargo check` is the only way to find every consumer.\n\n## 11. meta_lesson (P3 leftover: type-def change is not update-all-callsites)\n\nThe P3.5 wave's most significant deliverable is not the new closure-injectable helper — it's the **discovery of the P3 leftover** and the meta-lesson it teaches.\n\n- **In P3**: `GatewayDeps` was extended with 3 X3.5 fields. The P3 engineer inspected the workspace, found 6 in-crate construction sites in `pre_exec.rs`, and updated them with safe defaults. The 5 cross-crate callers in `touring-server/src/cli/exec.rs` were missed.\n- **In P3.5**: FASE 0 ran `cargo check --workspace` as the canonical gate. The compiler reported **5 E0063 missing-field errors** at the 5 cross-crate struct literals. The fix was mechanical and immediate.\n\nThe meta-lesson is operational, not theoretical:\n\n1. **Type-def changes require workspace-wide `cargo check`**, not in-crate inspection. The Rust compiler is the only tool that knows every consumer of a struct field — and a workspace build is the only way to exercise that knowledge.\n2. **The P3 wave's \"12 files modified\" count missed the cross-crate callers.** The P3 documentation listed \"5 dependent sites in sandbox_stage/learn/lib\" but did not list the 5 sites in `touring-server` because the P3 engineer did not run `cargo check --workspace` (or did, but missed the diagnostic in a long output stream).\n3. **FASE 0 is the canonical gate for type-def changes**, period. Any L3+ refactor that touches a public struct field MUST pass `cargo check --workspace` at FASE 0 — not at FASE 5 (implementation) and not at FASE 6 (audit). FASE 0 is the only phase where a compile-fail is *cheap* (no work has been done yet).\n\n**Counterfactual**: in a language without a strong type system, this kind of cross-crate breakage would be a *runtime* bug — a struct literal in `touring-server` would silently default to whatever the type's `Default::default()` returns (or crash with a runtime error). The Rust compiler caught all 5 sites in **<1 second** during `cargo check` — cheaper than a single test run.\n\n**Operational lesson for the next wave (P2.5 cvc5)**: any future type-def change in `touring-offensive::solver` (where `prove_claim` and friends live) MUST trigger a `cargo check --workspace` at FASE 0. The cvc5 backend will likely add a new variant to `SolverBackendKind`; that change will require updating every match arm that consumes the enum. The same FASE 0 discipline applies.\n\n## 12. next_recommendations\n\n1. **ES1 P2.5 — cvc5 0.4 migration** (~2ed, blocking on `libcvc5-dev` system dep). Activate the dormant `cvc5_backend.rs` using the same typed-AST pattern as ES1 P2. Independent SMT solver for cross-validation; useful for `RefactorEquivalence` claims where solver disagreement is informative. **Pre-flight**: run `cargo check --workspace` at FASE 0 — the new `SolverBackendKind::Cvc5` variant will require updating every match arm in `prove_claim`'s dispatch.\n2. **ES1 P4 — `claim_from_intent` helper** (~2ed). The P3 meta-lesson identified this as the next-level mechanism: given an `Action` from the speculative driver, derive the `ClaimKind` that should be proved. The P3 type system ensures prove_claim *runs*; P3.5 ensures the speculative driver *calls* it; P4 ensures it proves the *right* claim. **Closure-injectable design**: take the `Action` -> `Option<ClaimKind>` mapping as a `Fn` parameter, just like `filter_by_proof` takes the prover as a `Fn` parameter. This keeps the helper testable and the production wiring swappable.\n3. **ES3 P2 — `supervised.rs` X8 with WRITES** (~5ed). ES3 P1 made `txn_lock_enforcement` default-ON for *reads*; P2 makes the permit meaningful for *writes* (the actual OP4 §5.2.4 lost-update guard). Independent of ES1.\n4. **Re-run CAH oracle** to measure the `interface.formal-verify` row flip. Expected lift: 0.65 PARCIAL -> CONFORME ~0.85+ (matching ES1 P1+P4 + P2 + P3 + P3.5 predictions). Plus secondary rows (likely `op5-discharge-loop`, `harness-verifier-invocation`).\n5. **Backfill: re-audit P3 to confirm zero other call sites were missed**. The P3 leftover discovery in P3.5 raises the question: are there OTHER P3 type-def changes (in `offensive_integration`, `pre_exec.rs`, etc.) that have unfazed callers in other crates? A workspace-wide `cargo check` is the canonical answer; the audit should also include a manual grep for `GatewayDeps {` in every crate to confirm 0 stale literals.\n6. **`touring index rebuild` after P3.5** (~30s). The daemon's index was not rebuilt after the wave's edits; the `touring index find` query for `filter_by_proof` returns stale data. Not blocking — direct grep is authoritative — but downstream agents relying on `touring index find` will see stale results until rebuild.\n7. **Closure-injectable pattern as a TACO convention**. P3.5's `filter_by_proof<F: Fn(...)>` is a clean instance of \"function-as-parameter for testability\". The next 2-3 P-tier waves that introduce pure helpers should consider the same pattern: keep the I/O at the boundary, take the side-effecting function as a parameter. This makes the helper zero-cost (monomorphized) and 100% unit-testable without mocks.\n\n---\n\n**SEALING STATEMENT**: ES1 P3.5 SHIPPED 2026-06-02. S-12 speculative driver now CONSUMES X3.5 PROVE verdicts via `filter_by_proof` pre-pass. 13 verified symbols (4 speculative core + 1 modified run_gateway_speculative + 5 new unit tests + 3 new integration tests), 8 new tests, 0 regressions, 0 new orphans. 2.0/3ed consumed. **Strategic differentiator unlocked**: the X3.5 acceptance loop is closed — P3 made `prove_claim` callable, P3.5 made it *called*. **P3 leftover discovered and fixed**: 5 `GatewayDeps` struct literals in `touring-server/src/cli/exec.rs` were unfazed by P3's type-def change; caught at FASE 0 (5 E0063 errors) and fixed with safe defaults. **META-LESSON**: type-def changes are not update-all-callsites by inspection — FASE 0 (`cargo check --workspace`) is the canonical gate. **ES1 P2-P3 (15ed strategic differentiator) is now 15/15ed SHIPPED**. **Next strategic picks**: ES1 P2.5 (cvc5 — same FASE 0 discipline applies), ES1 P4 (claim_from_intent — closure-injectable design), ES3 P2 (supervised.rs X8 with WRITES).\n"
